/-!
# Radius-gap counts for active dyadic cells

The `TT*` proof for fractal dilations uses the *left endpoints* of dyadic
cells meeting the radius set.  Those endpoints need not belong to the radius
set, so the separated-sample lemma in `TTStarCovering` cannot be applied
directly.  This file supplies the corresponding counting statement directly
for active cells.

The only harmless price is an absolute factor `6`: a length-`δ` covering
interval meets at most six integer grid points after rescaling.  The proof is
written in this deliberately robust form to avoid any boundary ambiguity from
the closed-cell convention.
-/

namespace LeanSpherical.HarmonicAnalysis.FractalDilations

